The '''1978 FIFA World Cup final''' was a [[association football|football]] match played to determine the winner of the [[1978 FIFA World Cup]]. It was contested by teams from the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]] and the host country of [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] on 25 June 1978 at Argentina's largest stadium, the [[Estadio Monumental (Buenos Aires)|Estadio Monumental]] in [[Buenos Aires]]. The match was won by the Argentine team in extra time by a score of 3&ndash;1. [[Mario Kempes]], who finished as the tournament's top scorer, was named the man of the match. The Netherlands team lost their second consecutive World Cup final, both times to the host nation, after losing to [[West Germany national football team|West Germany]] in [[1974 FIFA World Cup|1974]].

